  "body": "### Summary\n\nA viewport fix for the way the camera eats the model from the inside.\n\nTwo ways the camera clipped the model while zooming:\n\n- **Perspective:** the near plane was a fixed 0.1 mm from the eye, so at close zoom the geometry right in front of the near plane clipped instead of rendering — zooming in went through the model. The near plane now rides `dist` (0.1 % of the view depth, clamped to 1e-5 min and 0.1 max).\n- **Orthographic:** `dist` moved the eye, so zooming dollied the eye into the model and clipped through its faces from inside. The eye now sits at a fixed nominal distance (100 mm) behind the target, and `dist` is only a zoom factor for the view box's half-height — the way it was always meant to work. The near plane now reaches far behind the eye plane: `-((dist * 20.0).max(1000.0) - ORTHO_EYE_DIST)`.\n\nChangelog: UI — the perspective near plane moves with the dolly distance and the orthographic camera's near plane no longer clips through geometry while zooming.\n\nThe tests pin the new ortho depth formula and a point in front of the eye plane (`dist = 300`, 150 mm back from the target), asserting it stays inside the clip volume.\n\n### Verification\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` — 803 passed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets` — clean. No posted G-code, collision check, stock simulation math or geometry changed.\n\nNo issue covers this viewport bug yet — a maintainer will file one.\n",
